  PRD 4 — T-04: Real-Time Canvas Audio Visualizer                               
  4.1 Git Commit                                                                
  feat(audio): implement performant real-time frequency visualizer              
                                                                                
  4.2 Objective                                                                 
  Build a real-time audio visualizer using Canvas or SVG, powered by the        
  AnalyserNode introduced in T-01.                                              
                                                                                
  The visualizer must update smoothly using requestAnimationFrame() while       
  avoiding unnecessary Mini-React state updates and repeated DOM                
  reconstruction.                                                               
                                                                                
  4.3 Functional Requirements                                                   
  FR-01: Create the Visualizer Interface                                        
  Add a semantic visualizer section to the application.                         
                                                                                
  The interface should include:                                                 
                                                                                
  A heading describing the visualizer.                                          
                                                                                
  A Canvas or SVG visualization surface.                                        
                                                                                
  A short status message indicating whether audio is loading, playing, or       
  stopped.                                                                      
                                                                                
  Accessible controls for playback and stopping audio, where appropriate.       
                                                                                
  A fallback message when audio is unavailable.                                 
                                                                                
  Use the existing Mini-React rendering engine to create the interface.         
                                                                                
  FR-02: Read Frequency Data                                                    
  Retrieve frequency data from the analyser using getByteFrequencyData() or an  
  appropriate equivalent.                                                       
                                                                                
  Reuse a typed array sized to analyser.frequencyBinCount.                      
                                                                                
  Do not allocate a new typed array on every animation frame.                   
                                                                                
  Read frequency data during the visualization loop.                            
                                                                                
  Handle the absence of an active analyser gracefully.                          
                                                                                
  FR-03: Render with requestAnimationFrame                                      
  Implement a dedicated animation loop that:                                    
                                                                                
  Reads the current frequency data.                                             
                                                                                
  Updates the Canvas or SVG visualization.                                      
                                                                                
  Schedules the next frame using requestAnimationFrame().                       
                                                                                
  Stops scheduling frames when visualization is no longer required.             
                                                                                
  Target approximately 60 FPS under normal browser conditions.                  
                                                                                
  Actual frame rates may vary depending on hardware, browser scheduling,        
  background-tab throttling, and rendering complexity.                          
                                                                                
  FR-04: Avoid State Thrashing                                                  
  The visualizer must not trigger a full Mini-React render for every animation  
  frame.                                                                        
                                                                                
  Draw directly to the Canvas rendering context, or update a small, controlled  
  set of SVG attributes.                                                        
                                                                                
  Keep the animation loop outside the application-wide state dispatcher.        
                                                                                
  Use UI state only for meaningful events, such as track selection, playback    
  status, or errors.                                                            
                                                                                
  Avoid unnecessary DOM creation and destruction.                               
                                                                                
  Reuse existing drawing objects and typed arrays where practical.              
                                                                                
  Canvas is preferred for a large number of frequency bars because it allows    
  efficient direct drawing without rebuilding DOM elements.                     
                                                                                
  FR-05: Visual Design                                                          
  Implement a frequency-bar visualizer or another clear representation of the   
  audio spectrum.                                                               
                                                                                
  The visualizer should:                                                        
                                                                                
  Scale to the available container width.                                       
                                                                                
  Adapt to Canvas size changes.                                                 
                                                                                
  Render a clear baseline when audio is stopped or no meaningful data is        
  available.                                                                    
                                                                                
  Avoid excessive visual complexity.                                            
                                                                                
  Remain usable at common desktop and mobile viewport sizes.                    
                                                                                
  FR-06: Stop and Clean Up Animation                                            
  The visualizer must:                                                          
                                                                                
  Store the active animation-frame identifier.                                  
                                                                                
  Cancel the animation frame when visualization is stopped or disposed.         
                                                                                
  Avoid starting duplicate animation loops.                                     
                                                                                
  Release registered resize listeners when they are no longer required.         
                                                                                
  Stop drawing when the associated component is no longer active.               
                                                                                
  When playback stops, either stop the animation loop or render a final         
  inactive frame and stop scheduling further frames.                            
                                                                                
  FR-07: Integrate with the Audio Engine                                        
  Connect the visualizer to the analyser provided by T-01.                      
                                                                                
  The visualizer must not create a separate audio engine or AudioContext for    
  each frame.                                                                   
                                                                                
  When a new track becomes active, the visualizer should continue using the     
  appropriate analyser and display the new frequency data without accumulating  
  animation loops.                                                              
                                                                                
  4.4 Non-Functional Requirements                                               
  Target approximately 60 FPS under normal conditions.                          
                                                                                
  Avoid per-frame Reactivity or full-tree rendering.                            
                                                                                
  Minimize allocations inside the animation loop.                               
                                                                                
  Avoid duplicate requestAnimationFrame() loops.                                
                                                                                
  Maintain correct behavior after track changes and cleanup.                    
                                                                                
  Preserve keyboard accessibility and meaningful status text.                   
                                                                                
  4.5 Acceptance Criteria                                                       
                                                                                
  The visualizer displays frequency data from the active audio source.          
                                                                                
                                                                                
  FFT configuration supports 256 or 512.                                        
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The visualizer updates using requestAnimationFrame().                         
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Canvas or SVG drawing does not cause a full Mini-React render per frame.      
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Typed arrays are reused rather than recreated continuously.                   
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Animation stops when requested or when the component is disposed.             
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Rapid track switching does not create duplicate animation loops.              
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The visualization scales to the available container dimensions.               
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The complete audio workflow works with the queue and cleanup mechanisms from  
  T-02 and T-03.                                                                
                                                                                
  4.6 Suggested Testing                                                         
  Play a valid track and observe the visualizer while monitoring browser        
  performance tools.                                                            
                                                                                
  Check that:                                                                   
                                                                                
  Frequency bars respond to changes in audio.                                   
                                                                                
  Playback remains responsive.                                                  
                                                                                
  The visualizer does not accumulate animation callbacks.                       
                                                                                
  Switching tracks does not create additional active loops.                     
                                                                                
  Stopping playback ends unnecessary rendering.                                 
                                                                                
  UI state updates remain separate from per-frame drawing.                      
                                                                                
  5. Final Integration and Verification                                         
  After completing all four commits, run an integration test against the        
  complete application.                                                         
                                                                                
  5.1 End-to-End Workflow                                                       
  Initialize the audio engine.                                                  
                                                                                
  Enqueue multiple audio tracks.                                                
                                                                                
  Verify FIFO download and decoding order.                                      
                                                                                
  Select a successfully decoded track.                                          
                                                                                
  Start playback through a user interaction.                                    
                                                                                
  Render frequency data using the analyser.                                     
                                                                                
  Switch to another track while the first is loading or playing.                
                                                                                
  Cancel obsolete requests and prevent stale results from taking effect.        
                                                                                
  Stop playback and verify source-node cleanup.                                 
                                                                                
  Dispose of the engine and verify that pending work and animation frames are   
  cleaned up.                                                                   
                                                                                
  5.2 Final Acceptance Checklist                                                
                                                                                
  All four commits exist separately and in the intended order.                  
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The Web Audio API integration works.                                          
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The analyser uses an FFT size of 256 or 512.                                  
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The FIFO queue handles simultaneous track requests.                           
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Downloads and decoding follow the queue's documented scheduling policy.       
                                                                                
                                                                                
  AbortController cancels cancellable network requests.                         
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Stale asynchronous results are safely ignored.                                
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Audio source nodes are explicitly cleaned up.                                 
                                                                                
                                                                                
  The visualizer uses requestAnimationFrame().                                  
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Per-frame visualization does not trigger full application renders.            
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Animation loops and listeners are cleaned up.                                 
                                                                                
                                                                                
  Existing Mini-React functionality remains intact.                             
                                                                                
                                                                                
  All changes are committed with clear, descriptive messages.                   
                                                                                
  5.3 Recommended Commit Sequence                                               
  Commit    Milestone    Commit message                                         
  1    T-01    feat(audio): implement Web Audio engine and analyser             
  2    T-02    feat(audio): implement FIFO loading and decoding queue           
  3    T-03    fix(audio): prevent resource leaks and cancel stale requests     
  4    T-04    feat(audio): implement performant real-time frequency visualizer 
  Definition of Done: The project can load and decode audio tracks in FIFO      
  order, play the selected track, visualize its frequency spectrum in real      
  time, cancel obsolete network operations, and clean up owned audio and        
  rendering resources without breaking the existing Mini-React application.     

