● The real-time spectrum visualizer (T-04) is built and committed as ded4b61 
  feat(audio): implement performant real-time frequency visualizer. All 97 audio
  tests pass in headless Edge, and the Data-Grid suite still passes 101/101.

  Something to know first: the last commit (b30e539) moved the audio folder from
  LAB2/AUDIO to LAB2/HW/audio but left the imports pointing at
  ../../HW/source/, which no longer exists. As a result, the demo and test pages
  had stopped loading at all. I changed those imports to ../../source/ in this
  commit.

  What T-04 adds:
  - New file audioVisualizer.js: draws the spectrum as bars on a <canvas>, one
    frame at a time with requestAnimationFrame. Each frame reuses the same
    frequency array from the engine. Nothing in the page's HTML changes per
    frame; a test watches the page for 60 frames and sees no changes.
  - Only ever one loop: pressing Play twice or switching tracks doesn't start a
    second one. Stop, the track ending, a track switch, or closing the player
    all stop it and leave a flat baseline. The loop also stops by itself as soon
    as nothing is playing.
  - Cleanup: closing the player or the audio engine (including directly through
    the engine) cancels the pending frame and removes the resize watcher.
  - Resizing: the canvas follows the width of its container and sharpens on
    high-resolution screens. When there are more frequency bins than room,
    neighbouring bins share one bar showing their highest value, so bars stay
    crisp.
  - Player changes: a new "Frequency spectrum" section with a heading, a canvas
    screen readers can name, fallback text for browsers without canvas, a short
    status line, and a button to switch the FFT size between 512 and 256.

  Testing:
  - New tests: I added 22 (14 for the visualizer, 8 in the player tests). They
    count pending frames exactly and check pixel colours on the canvas.
  - Mutation checks: removing the "only one loop" guard made 3 tests fail. Not
    stopping the visualizer on a track switch made 1 fail.
  - Demo in a real browser: at about 1000px and 500px wide, bars move while the
    tone plays and Stop works. There are no console errors and no sideways
    scrolling.

  Two things to watch:
  - Two tests play real audio. Browsers block audio until the page is clicked,
    so in a normal browser they may fail with a "suspended" message; click the
    page and reload. I ran them headless with
    --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required.
  - Your history has T-02 and T-03 committed twice each (ed2fe0d/1cbc557 and
    af3953d/b30e539). The order is still T-01 → T-04, but if the assignment
    wants exactly four commits you may want to squash those duplicates. I didn't
    rewrite history.

  report.md now has a T-04 section, the final integration walkthrough and
  checklist, a screenshot (LAB2/HW/audio/images/t04-visualizer.png), and
  corrected demo/test URLs: http://localhost:8765/HW/audio/source/…, served from
  the LAB2/ folder.

