● The first Mega-Sale task (T-01) is done and committed as c90b0a4 feat(sale): 
  establish mega-sale simulation foundation. All 21 new tests pass in headless
  Edge, and the Data-Grid (101/101) and audio (97/97) suites still pass.

  Where it lives: LAB2/HW/megasale/, laid out like audio/. It uses the existing
  Mini-React core in LAB2/HW/source/, wired up the same way as the Data-Grid and
  audio player, with state kept per mount. The repo has no main.js or index.js,
  so I didn't invent one.

  What T-01 covers:
  - One central config (saleConfig.js): campaign name, product, original and
    sale price, stock, start time and lock duration. Times are in epoch
    milliseconds and prices in whole đồng.
  - Bad config doesn't crash the page: every problem is listed at once in an
    alert box, and no product card is built from the bad data.
  - Status is calculated, never stored (saleStatus.js): UPCOMING, LIVE or ENDED
    comes from the schedule and the current time each time it's needed. Tests
    check the exact switch-over moments, 1 ms on either side.
  - Product card: both prices are labelled in text ("Original price", "Sale
    price"), because screen readers don't announce strikethrough. It also shows
    the discount, units left, status and sale window.
  - Main button follows the status: "Opens at HH:mm", "Reserve now", "Sold out"
    or "Sale ended". For now, Reserve only displays a message that reservations
    aren't available yet; the real reservation logic comes in a later task.

  Project rules (Project_Rule.md):
  1. No divs: only semantic tags such as article, dl, output, time and button.
  2. Type checks: every argument and config value is checked.
  3. No innerHTML: all text goes through textContent; a product name containing
     <img onerror> shows as plain text.
  4. One mount: everything is mounted through renderToDOM.

  Decisions for you to check:
  - I added an end time (endsAt) to the config. The PRD's field list has no end
    time, but ENDED can't be worked out without one.
  - I made one small change to the shared core: lang is now an allowed attribute
    in renderToDOM.js, so Vietnamese text can be marked lang="vi" for screen
    readers. Nothing else in the core changed.
  - The sample sale is scheduled relative to now, starting in 2 minutes and
    running for 30. A fixed 11.11 date would show "Upcoming" or "Ended" for most
    of the year. The demo has links for each scenario: ?scenario=upcoming,
    live, ended and invalid.

  To check that the tests can actually fail, I briefly broke the code twice.
  Opening the sale 1 ms late made 5 tests fail, and accepting any number as
  stock made 3 fail. All four demo scenarios also render correctly at 900px and
  375px wide, with no console errors and no sideways scrolling. Details and
  screenshots are in LAB2/HW/megasale/report.md.

  The audit files from last turn (AI_AUDIT_FAILURE_2.md and the related audio
  edits) are still uncommitted, and I kept them out of this commit. Do you want
  them committed separately?

