      119 +                                                              
      120 +## T-02 — Zero-drift millisecond countdown                    
      121 +                                                              
      122 +Commit: `feat(timer): implement zero-drift sale countdown`    
      123 +                                                              
      124 +| File | Change |                                             
      125 +| --- | --- |                                                 
      126 +| `source/countdown.js` | `remainingMs(target, now)`, `formatD
          +uration(ms)` (HH:MM:SS.mmm), `createCountdown({ getTarget, onT
          +ick, onReached })` with `start` / `stop` / `dispose` |        
      127 +| `source/productCard.js` | Countdown line: label plus `<time 
          +role="timer">`; sale window shows seconds |                   
      128 +| `source/mountMegaSale.js` | One countdown per mount: to `sta
          +rtsAt` while UPCOMING, to `endsAt` while LIVE; status change a
          +t the target; `options.timer` for tests |                     
      129 +| `source/megaSale.demo.html` | `?scenario=soon`: starts 5 s a
          +fter load, ends 15 s later. The T-01 "Re-check status" button 
          +is gone because the countdown now updates the status |        
      130 +                                                              
      131 +![Live countdown after the sale opened](images/t02-live-countd
          +own.png)                                                      
      132 +                                                              
      133 +Key decisions:                                                
      134 +                                                              
      135 +- **The wall clock is the only source of time.** Every update 
          +computes                                                      
      136 +  `Math.max(0, target - now())`. `setInterval` (50 ms) only de
          +cides when                                                    
      137 +  the display refreshes; nothing is counted or decremented. A 
          +test moves the                                                
      138 +  fake clock by 50, 13, 400 and 7 ms between ticks and checks 
          +each value is                                                 
      139 +  exactly `target - now`. Another lets 25 minutes pass with a 
          +single                                                        
      140 +  callback (a throttled tab or a sleeping device) and checks t
          +he display                                                    
      141 +  reads `00:34:59.950`.                                       
      142 +- **`setInterval`, not `requestAnimationFrame`.** Browsers pau
          +se                                                            
      143 +  `requestAnimationFrame` completely in background tabs. The s
          +ale would                                                     
      144 +  then not switch to LIVE until the tab became visible again. 
      145 +  `setInterval` is throttled in background tabs (to about 1 s)
          + but still                                                    
      146 +  runs, and because values come from the clock, the throttling
          + causes no                                                    
      147 +  drift.                                                      
