● Update(LAB2\HW\megasale\report.md)
  ⎿  Added 118 lines
      204  | --- | --- |
      205  | Card re-rendered on every tick | 5 |
      206  | Remaining time from `firstTick + updates × 50 ms` (an interv
           al counter) instead of `Date.now()` | 8 |
      207 +                                                              
      208 +## T-03 — Inventory reservation finite state machine          
      209 +                                                              
      210 +Commit: `feat(inventory): implement reservation state machine`
      211 +                                                              
      212 +| File | Change |                                             
      213 +| --- | --- |                                                 
      214 +| `source/reservationMachine.js` | `RESERVATION_STATE` (7 stat
          +es), `RESERVATION_EVENT`, the frozen `TRANSITIONS` table, `tra
          +nsition(state, event)`, `canTransition`, `ReservationError` wi
          +th codes |                                                    
      215 +| `source/inventory.js` | `createInventory(total)`: `reserve` 
          +/ `release` / `commit` between the available, reserved and sol
          +d buckets; `assertInventoryInvariant` |                       
      216 +| `source/reservationStore.js` | The authoritative controller:
          + `reserve`, `beginCheckout`, `completeCheckout`, `failCheckout
          +`, `cancel`, `expire`, `activeFor`, `subscribe` |             
      217 +| `source/saleConfig.js` | Adds `productId` (lowercase letters
          +, digits, hyphens), which every reservation records |         
      218 +| `source/productCard.js` | Available / Reserved / Sold rows; 
          +reserve form (labelled quantity field + submit); reservation p
          +anel (id, state, quantity, lock end, Cancel) |                
      219 +| `source/mountMegaSale.js` | One store per mount; the card re
          +-renders from store snapshots on every accepted change; focus 
          +is restored by `data-focus` key |                             
      220 +                                                              
      221 +![A locked reservation](images/t03-reserved.png)              
      222 +                                                              
      223 +Key decisions:                                                
      224 +                                                              
      225 +- **One table of transitions.** `TRANSITIONS` maps each state 
          +to the events                                                 
      226 +  it accepts, with exactly the nine moves in the PRD.         
      227 +  `transition(state, event)` returns the next state or throws 
      228 +  `ReservationError("invalid-transition")`. A test walks all 5
          +6                                                             
      229 +  (state, event) pairs: 9 are allowed and the other 47 are rej
          +ected.                                                        
      230 +  `PURCHASED`, `EXPIRED` and `CANCELLED` have empty rows, so a
          +n expired or                                                  
      231 +  cancelled reservation can never reach checkout or purchase. 
      232 +- **A reservation is a record, not a flag.** It has `id`, `pro
          +ductId`,                                                      
      233 +  `shopperId`, `quantity`, `createdAt`, `expiresAt` (set when 
          +it locks),                                                    
      234 +  `updatedAt`, `state` and `failure`. The store hands out froz
          +en snapshots;                                                 
      235 +  only the store changes records, and only through `transition
          +()`. Ids come                                                 
      236 +  from `crypto.randomUUID()` (tests inject a counter), and the
          + store                                                        
      237 +  refuses an id it has seen before.                           
      238 +- **Inventory buckets.** `total = available + reserved + sold`
          +, all                                                         
      239 +  non-negative safe integers. Stock only moves between buckets
          + (reserve,                                                    
      240 +  release, commit). Each move checks its quantity first and ch
          +anges nothing                                                 
      241 +  when rejected. The invariant is asserted after every accepte
          +d move, and                                                   
      242 +  every store notification passes a snapshot that the tests ch
          +eck.                                                          
      243 +- **Reserve, in PRD order.** (1) The sale is LIVE, (2) the qua
          +ntity is a                                                    
      244 +  whole number ≥ 1, (3) enough stock is available, (4) the sho
          +pper has no                                                   
      245 +  active reservation. Only then is a record created and moved 
      246 +  `IDLE → RESERVING`. After the simulated processing step (400
          + ms in the                                                    
      247 +  demo, instant in tests), checks 1 and 3 run again, because t
          +ime and stock                                                 
      248 +  can change while a request is in flight. Then `inventory.res
          +erve()` runs                                                  
      249 +  and the record moves `RESERVING → LOCKED` with              
      250 +  `expiresAt = now + lockDurationMs`. Rejections in steps 1–4 
          +create                                                        
      251 +  nothing and touch no stock. A failure after RESERVING moves 
          +it back to                                                    
      252 +  `IDLE` with the reason; stock was never taken on that path. 
      253 +- **Stock is taken at lock time, not request time.** Two shopp
          +ers can both                                                  
      254 +  pass the first check for the last units. The one whose proce
          +ssing                                                         
      255 +  finishes first gets the lock; the other fails back to IDLE w
          +ith "Only 1                                                   
      256 +  unit is available." Nothing is oversold, and a failed reserv
          +ation never                                                   
      257 +  decrements `available`.                                     
      258 +- **No double reservation.** A request that would reserve twic
          +e is                                                          
      259 +  rejected as `duplicate-reservation` while the shopper has a 
          +`RESERVING`,                                                  
      260 +  `LOCKED` or `CHECKING_OUT` reservation. In the UI the form i
          +s replaced by                                                 
      261 +  the "Reserving…" panel as soon as it is submitted, so a seco
          +nd click has                                                  
      262 +  nothing to submit. A test also calls the store directly to c
          +heck the                                                      
      263 +  second layer.                                               
      264 +- **Checkout guard.** `beginCheckout` accepts only `LOCKED`. A
          + lock whose                                                   
      265 +  `expiresAt` has passed is expired on the spot (stock release
          +d) and the                                                    
      266 +  call is rejected. The same applies to `completeCheckout`, so
          + a checkout                                                   
      267 +  that outlives its lock ends `EXPIRED`, never `PURCHASED`. Ex
          +piry is lazy                                                  
      268 +  in T-03; a timer that expires locks on its own belongs to a 
          +later                                                         
      269 +  milestone. The checkout methods exist and are tested, but th
          +e checkout                                                    
      270 +  screen is not built yet.                                    
      271 +- **Errors the user can act on.** Every rejection is a `Reserv
          +ationError`                                                   
      272 +  with a stable `code` (`not-live`, `sale-ended`, `invalid-qua
          +ntity`,                                                       
      273 +  `insufficient-stock`, `duplicate-reservation`, `not-found`, 
      274 +  `invalid-transition`, `reservation-expired`, `processing-fai
          +led`) and a                                                   
      275 +  plain message, shown in the live region as "Could not reserv
          +e: …". An                                                     
      276 +  unexpected error in processing is wrapped as `processing-fai
          +led` and                                                      
      277 +  keeps the original as `cause`.                              
      278 +- **UI.** A live sale with stock shows a `<form>` with a label
          +led                                                           
      279 +  `<input type="number" min="1" max="available">` and a submit
          + button. Enter                                                
      280 +  submits, and the default page reload is prevented. The typed
          + value is                                                     
      281 +  kept across re-renders. An active reservation shows a `<sect
          +ion>` with                                                    
      282 +  its id, state, quantity, lock end (`<time>`) and a Cancel bu
          +tton, enabled                                                 
      283 +  only while LOCKED. After reserving, focus moves to Cancel; a
          +fter                                                          
      284 +  cancelling, it moves back to the first control.             
      285 +- **Scope.** The store is in-memory and per page. It keeps sto
          +ck                                                            
      286 +  consistent for the reservations it sees, including several s
          +hoppers in                                                    
      287 +  one page, but it cannot coordinate browsers or devices. It i
          +s a                                                           
      288 +  simulation, not an inventory service.                       
      289 +                                                              
      290 +Tests: `source/megaSale.test.html` — 73/73 passed (headless Ed
          +ge 155). The                                                  
      291 +24 store-and-machine tests cover the state list and frozen tab
          +le, every                                                     
      292 +allowed and every rejected (state, event) pair, terminal state
          +s,                                                            
      293 +inventory moves and rejected overdrafts, the invariant checker
          +, the                                                         
