● PRD 2 (countdown) and PRD 3 (reservation state machine) are both done and
  committed, one commit each. The Mega-Sale tests pass 73/73, and the Data-Grid
  (101/101) and audio (97/97) suites still pass.

  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┐
  │                   Commit                   │            What            │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
  │ 63ca5a2 feat(timer): implement zero-drift  │ T-02                       │
  │ sale countdown                             │                            │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
  │ 15c0006 feat(inventory): implement         │ T-03                       │
  │ reservation state machine                  │                            │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
  │ a739d94 test(audio): keep mutation records │ Fix for a bug in the audio │
  │  the observer callback receives            │  tests, found during T-02  │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┘

  T-02 — Countdown
  - No drift: every update works out the time left from the real clock
    (Math.max(0, target − Date.now())). The 50 ms timer only decides when the
    screen refreshes; nothing is counted down. A test jumps the clock 25 minutes
    with a single callback, like a background tab or a sleeping laptop, and the
    display is still exact.
  - Why setInterval and not requestAnimationFrame: browsers stop
    requestAnimationFrame entirely in background tabs, so the sale would only go
    live once the tab came back into view.
  - Display: shows HH:MM:SS.mmm, never goes negative, and hours keep counting
    past 99.
  - Status changes: at the start the sale switches to Live and announces it,
    then counts down to the end. At the end it shows 00:00:00.000 and the timer
    stops. If the device sleeps through the whole sale, the next update goes
    straight to Ended.
  - Light on the page: each update only rewrites the countdown text; the card is
    redrawn only when the status changes. Screen readers don't read the
    20-per-second updates aloud, only the status changes.

  T-03 — Reservations
  - Allowed moves: one table lists exactly the 9 moves from the PRD. A test
    tries all 56 combinations of state and event, and the other 47 are rejected.
    That means an expired or cancelled reservation can never be bought.
  - Stock always adds up: total = available + reserved + sold, all whole numbers
    that never go negative, checked after every change.
  - One place changes stock: a reservation is only created after four checks
    pass: the sale is live, the quantity is valid, there's enough stock, and you
    don't already hold a reservation. Time and stock are checked again just
    before the units are locked.
    - Never oversold: if two shoppers race for the last units, the loser goes
      back to "no reservation" and takes nothing.
  - Checkout: only a locked reservation can start checkout. If its lock time has
    already passed, it expires on the spot and the stock is released.
  - On the page: the card shows Available, Reserved and Sold, a labelled
    quantity field with a Reserve button, and your current reservation (ID,
    state, quantity, lock end time) with a Cancel button.

  Decisions to check
  - productId added to the config: PRD 3 requires a product ID on every
    reservation, so I added it.
  - Expiry and checkout are only partly built: a passed lock expires when
    someone tries to check out, and the checkout logic is tested, but nothing
    expires locks automatically and there's no checkout screen yet. I expect
    both in later PRDs.
  - Simulated delay: reserving waits 400 ms in the demo (instant in tests) so
    you can see the "Reserving…" step.

  Test bugs I found and fixed
  - "Nothing on the page changed" checks: these could never fail, because the
    change records were used up before the test read them. I fixed this in
    Mega-Sale and in the audio tests from earlier (a739d94). If you add to
    AI_AUDIT_FAILURE_2.md, this belongs there.
  - Hang instead of failure: when I deliberately removed the
    duplicate-reservation check, one test hung forever instead of failing. It
    now has a time limit.

  To confirm the tests actually catch mistakes, I broke the code on purpose 6
  times, for example letting an expired reservation reach checkout or computing
  time from the timer instead of the clock. Every break made at least one test
  fail. Both new features also work in the demo at desktop and phone widths,
  with no console errors. Details are in LAB2/HW/megasale/report.md.

  Repo changes I didn't make
  - Commit 02b67d6: it contains the audit files but reuses the T-01 message
    feat(sale): establish mega-sale simulation foundation.
  - Deleted files: LAB2/HW/report.md and
    LAB2/EXERCISE/sources/lulehuonggiang_24520416.pdf are deleted, and there's a
    new untracked lulehuonggiang_24520416.fs.pdf.

  I kept all of these out of my commits. You now have 4 Mega-Sale commits toward
  the required 8, including your 02b67d6; it counts only if you keep it as is.

