● Update(LAB2\HW\megasale\report.md)
  ⎿  Added 90 lines
      322  The duplicate mutation first made the suite hang instead of fa
           il: the
      323  test awaited a second reservation whose processing never finis
           hed. That
      324  await is now raced against one tick.
      325 +                                                              
      326 +## T-04 — Optimistic inventory lock and expiry                
      327 +                                                              
      328 +Commit: `feat(inventory): add expiring inventory reservation l
          +ocks`                                                         
      329 +                                                              
      330 +| File | Change |                                             
      331 +| --- | --- |                                                 
      332 +| `source/reservationStore.js` | One expiry timer per LOCKED r
          +eservation; `expireIfDue(id)` (idempotent) and `sweepExpired()
          +` replace T-03's unconditional `expire(id)`; `reserve()` sweep
          +s due locks first; `cancel()` on a due lock expires it instead
          +; injectable `setTimeout` / `clearTimeout` |                  
      333 +| `source/productCard.js` | "Lock expires in HH:MM:SS.mmm" (`<
          +time role="timer">`) in the reservation panel |               
      334 +| `source/mountMegaSale.js` | A second, display-only countdown
          + for the active lock; expiry announcement; `options.timer.setT
          +imeout` / `clearTimeout` go to the store |                    
      335 +| `source/megaSale.demo.html` | `?scenario=short-lock`: a live
          + sale with a 20-second lock, to watch a reservation expire |  
      336 +                                                              
      337 +Key decisions:                                                
      338 +                                                              
      339 +- **Absolute expiry.** A lock records `createdAt` and         
      340 +  `expiresAt = lock time + lockDurationMs` (5 minutes in the s
          +ample). It is                                                 
      341 +  valid while `now < expiresAt`, and every check reads the clo
          +ck. At exactly                                                
      342 +  `expiresAt` the lock is no longer eligible for checkout, eve
          +n if no timer                                                 
      343 +  has run yet (tested with no timer fired).                   
      344 +- **Release exactly once.** Stock from an expired lock is rele
          +ased only by                                                  
      345 +  the `LOCKED → EXPIRED` transition. `expireLockIfDue` checks 
          +that the                                                      
      346 +  reservation is LOCKED and due, validates the transition, the
          +n releases                                                    
      347 +  and applies it with no `await` in between. Because the trans
          +ition can                                                     
      348 +  happen once, repeated `expireIfDue` calls, a sweep and a lat
          +e timer                                                       
      349 +  release nothing more (`expired: false`). T-03's `expire(id)`
          + released                                                     
      350 +  stock without checking that the lock was due; it has been re
          +moved.                                                        
      351 +- **Stale callbacks.** The timer callback carries the reservat
          +ion id and                                                    
      352 +  the `expiresAt` it was armed for. It does nothing unless tha
          +t reservation                                                 
      353 +  still exists, still has that `expiresAt` and is still LOCKED
          +. Timers are                                                  
      354 +  also cleared on checkout, cancel and purchase. The tests use
          + a "leaky"                                                    
      355 +  timer whose `clearTimeout` does nothing, so every old callba
          +ck really                                                     
      356 +  runs: it cannot expire a cancelled reservation, a purchased 
          +one, or the                                                   
      357 +  newer reservation that replaced it.                         
      358 +- **Early and late timers.** Browsers can fire timers early (r
          +arely) or very                                                
      359 +  late (background tabs, sleep). An early callback re-arms for
          + the time                                                     
      360 +  left. A late one expires the lock once. `reserve()` first sw
          +eeps every                                                    
      361 +  due lock, so a delayed timer never makes the next shopper se
          +e "sold out"                                                  
      362 +  for stock that should already be free.                      
      363 +- **Timer only while LOCKED.** `beginCheckout` disarms it and 
          +a failed                                                      
      364 +  checkout re-arms it for the *original* expiry (not a fresh 5
          + minutes). A                                                  
      365 +  lock that runs out during checkout is expired by the checkou
          +t itself.                                                     
      366 +- **Cancellation.** `LOCKED → CANCELLED` releases stock once. 
          +A second                                                      
      367 +  cancel, checkout or expiry of that reservation is rejected o
          +r does                                                        
      368 +  nothing. Cancelling at or after `expiresAt` expires it inste
          +ad, so the                                                    
      369 +  stock is still released once and the state tells the truth. 
      370 +- **Indivisible operations.** Every method that changes stock 
          +goes from its                                                 
      371 +  last validation to its last write synchronously: JavaScript 
          +runs one task                                                 
      372 +  at a time, so nothing can interleave. `reserve()` awaits onl
          +y the                                                         
      373 +  simulated processing step and validates time and stock again
          + after it.                                                    
      374 +  The UI has no handler that changes counts; it only calls the
          + store.                                                       
      375 +- **Display.** The panel shows "Lock expires in 00:04:59.950",
          + computed                                                     
      376 +  from `expiresAt` by a second zero-drift countdown that only 
          +displays.                                                     
      377 +  When that countdown reaches the lock's `expiresAt`, it asks 
          +the store to                                                  
      378 +  `expireIfDue` *that* reservation (it remembers the id). This
          + covers a                                                     
      379 +  delayed store timer and is harmless if the timer already ran
          +. Expiry is                                                   
      380 +  announced: "Your reservation expired. 2 units went back to a
          +vailable                                                      
      381 +  stock."                                                     
      382 +- **Limitation.** This is in-process consistency for one page.
          + Real                                                         
      383 +  inventory locking across clients needs server-side atomic op
          +erations,                                                     
      384 +  durable reservation records and transactions.               
      385 +                                                              
      386 +Tests: `source/megaSale.test.html` — 91/91 passed (headless Ed
          +ge 155). The                                                  
      387 +14 new store tests cover: lock creation; validity 1 ms before 
          +and at                                                        
      388 +`expiresAt`; the timer expiring and releasing; early timers re
          +-arming; very                                                 
      389 +late timers; idempotent `expireIfDue` with repeated calls, a s
          +weep and a                                                    
      390 +late timer; stale callbacks after cancel-and-replace and after
          + purchase;                                                    
      391 +cancel releasing once; cancel at the expiry time; a delayed ti
          +mer not                                                       
      392 +blocking the next shopper; three shoppers competing for the la
          +st units;                                                     
      393 +disarm and re-arm around checkout; and `dispose()` clearing ti
          +mers. Four UI                                                 
      394 +tests cover the lock countdown (timer role, recomputed from th
          +e clock),                                                     
      395 +expiry by the store timer (panel removed, stock back, announce
          +ment),                                                        
      396 +expiry by the display countdown when the store timer is late (
          +and no                                                        
      397 +second release when it finally fires), and the lock countdown 
          +stopping on                                                   
      398 +cancel. A store listener in the lock tests checks the invarian
          +t after                                                       
      399 +every change and records every release.                       
      400 +                                                              
      401 +Demo check: `?scenario=short-lock` shows "Lock expires in 00:0
          +0:17.344" 3 s                                                 
      402 +after reserving. After 22 s the panel is gone, stock is back t
          +o 50 and the                                                  
      403 +live region says "Your reservation expired. 1 unit went back t
          +o available                                                   
      404 +stock." There are no console errors.                          
      405 +                                                              
      406 +Mutation checks (each made tests fail, then the code was resto
          +red):                                                         
      407 +                                                              
      408 +| Mutation | Failing tests |                                  
      409 +| --- | --- |                                                 
      410 +| Expiry releases stock without checking the reservation state
          + | 33 |                                                       
      411 +| `beginCheckout` trusts LOCKED without checking `expiresAt` |
          + 2 |                                                          
      412 +| Timer callback skips the identity / state check | 3 |       
      413 +| `reserve()` does not sweep due locks first | 1 |            
      414 +| Re-armed timer gets a fresh full lock duration | 2 |        

