      498 +                                                              
      499 +## T-06 — Sale UI integration and race-condition hardening    
      500 +                                                              
      501 +Commit: `fix(sale): prevent timer and inventory state inconsis
          +tencies`                                                      
      502 +                                                              
      503 +Method: I first wrote `source/integration.test.js`, which driv
          +es the                                                        
      504 +whole simulator (fake clock, manual timers, real DOM) through 
          +the PRD 6                                                     
      505 +scenarios, and ran it against the T-05 code. Five of its 11 te
          +sts failed.                                                   
      506 +These are the defects this milestone fixes:                   
      507 +                                                              
      508 +| # | Failing test (before the fix) | Defect |                
      509 +| --- | --- | --- |                                           
      510 +| 1 | returning to the tab after the lock ran out expires it a
          +t once, even if no timer has run | Nothing re-checked locks wh
          +en the page became visible. Throttled timers left an expired l
          +ock showing "Reserved (locked)" and its stock unavailable unti
          +l a timer or tick finally ran |                               
      511 +| 2 | the sale ending during an active lock keeps the reservat
          +ion and says so | The end announcement was just "The sale has 
          +ended.", which suggests the shopper's held reservation is gone
          +, although it stays valid until its own expiry |              
      512 +| 3 | before the start: … reservations unavailable with a reas
          +on | Disabled Reserve had only a short label ("Opens at 00:05"
          +), with no explanation linked to it |                         
      513 +| 4 | after the end, a sale with no active lock refuses new re
          +servations and explains why | Same, for "Sale ended" and "Sold
          + out" |                                                       
      514 +| 5 | disabled Checkout and Cancel explain why while a reserva
          +tion or payment is in progress | Checkout / Cancel were disabl
          +ed during RESERVING and CHECKING_OUT with no reason |         
      515 +                                                              
      516 +| File | Change |                                             
      517 +| --- | --- |                                                 
      518 +| `source/mountMegaSale.js` | `visibilitychange` → `store.swee
          +pExpired()` (listener removed on dispose); end-of-sale announc
          +ement mentions a held lock and its end time; the purchase conf
          +irmation is read from the store by reservation id instead of a
          + kept snapshot |                                              
      519 +| `source/productCard.js` | `primaryAction` and `panelReason` 
          +return a reason for every disabled action; a visible `<p class
          +="sale-reason">` linked with `aria-describedby` |             
      520 +| `source/megaSale.css` | `.sale-reason` |                    
      521 +| `source/integration.test.js` | 11 whole-simulator tests for 
          +the PRD 6 scenarios |                                         
      522 +                                                              
      523 +Key decisions:                                                
      524 +                                                              
      525 +- **Single source of truth.** Every number and state on the ca
          +rd is read                                                    
      526 +  from the store when the card renders: stock buckets, the act
          +ive                                                           
      527 +  reservation and, now, the purchase confirmation (`store.get(
          +id)`). The UI                                                 
      528 +  keeps only the typed quantity and the id of the last purchas
          +e. A test                                                     
      529 +  checks that the confirmation always refers to a PURCHASED re
          +cord.                                                         
      530 +- **Resume.** Countdowns already recompute from the clock on t
          +he next tick.                                                 
      531 +  Locks are now also validated when the tab becomes visible ag
          +ain:                                                          
      532 +  `sweepExpired()` expires every due lock at once, releases it
          +s stock once                                                  
      533 +  and announces it. A test advances the clock past the lock wi
          +th no timer                                                   
      534 +  or tick, fires `visibilitychange` and checks the lock is gon
          +e, then fires                                                 
      535 +  the late timers and ticks and checks nothing changes.       
      536 +- **Expiry vs. checkout ordering.** Both paths validate the sa
          +me record                                                     
      537 +  against the current time and state before touching stock (T-
          +04/T-05).                                                     
      538 +  The integration tests confirm it end to end: checkout 1 ms b
          +efore                                                         
      539 +  `expiresAt` sells; at `expiresAt` it does not, even with no 
          +timer run.                                                    
      540 +  Cancel 1 ms before expiry releases once, and the expiry that
          + follows                                                      
      541 +  changes nothing.                                            
      542 +- **Identity.** A replaced reservation is unaffected by the ol
          +d lock's                                                      
      543 +  countdown and timer, and the panel shows the new id.        
      544 +- **Campaign end.** New reservations stop and the Reserve butt
          +on explains                                                   
      545 +  why. A lock held at the end stays, its stock stays reserved,
          + and the                                                      
      546 +  announcement says "The sale has ended. Your reservation of 2
          + units is                                                     
      547 +  still held until 00:42:10; you can still check out."        
      548 +- **Accessible feedback.** Every disabled action now has a vis
          +ible reason                                                   
      549 +  linked by `aria-describedby`:                               
      550 +  - before the start: "Reservations open when the sale starts 
          +at …"                                                         
      551 +  - sold out: "All units are reserved or sold. Units come back
          + if a                                                         
      552 +    reservation expires or is cancelled."                     
      553 +  - ended: "The sale has ended, so new reservations are closed
          +."                                                            
      554 +  - reserving: "Checkout and cancel become available once your
      555 +    reservation is confirmed."                                
      556 +  - paying: "Your payment is being processed. You cannot cance
          +l during                                                      
      557 +    payment; if it fails, your reservation stays held."       
      558 +                                                              
      559 +  Status changes go to the one `role="status"` region; the two
      560 +  countdowns are `role="timer"` and are never announced per ti
          +ck.                                                           
      561 +                                                              
      562 +Tests: `source/megaSale.test.html` — 116/116 passed (headless 
          +Edge 155). The                                                
      563 +11 integration tests cover the upcoming state with a reason; t
          +he sale ending                                                
      564 +during a lock (kept, announced, still purchasable); refusal af
          +ter the end                                                   
      565 +with a reason; resuming a tab after the lock ran out; reasons 
          +on disabled                                                   
      566 +Checkout and Cancel; five rapid reserve clicks making one rese
          +rvation;                                                      
      567 +checkout 1 ms before and exactly at expiry; cancel just before
          + expiry                                                       
      568 +followed by the expiry timer; a replaced reservation and the o
          +ld lock's                                                     
      569 +callbacks; the confirmation matching the store; and `dispose()
          +` removing                                                    
      570 +the same `visibilitychange` listener it added. Every store cha
          +nge in these                                                  
      571 +tests is checked against the inventory invariant.             
      572 +                                                              
      573 +![Disabled Reserve with its reason](images/t06-reason.png)    

