● PRDs 4 to 8 are done, so the whole Mega-Sale project is finished. Each
  milestone has its own commit, and all eight milestone commits are in history
  in the required order. The Mega-Sale tests pass 126/126, stable over 4 runs.
  All the older suites still pass: Data-Grid 101, audio 97, and the
  createElement, events and todo pages 18, 9 and 7.

  #: 4
  Commit: 193b7f1 feat(inventory): add expiring inventory reservation locks
  What it adds: Each lock gets a timer for its fixed expiry time, and expired
  stock is released exactly once. Old timer callbacks are ignored, and the
  panel shows the lock's countdown.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 5
  Commit: ef08772 feat(checkout): implement reservation checkout workflow
  What it adds: Checks before checkout, then a simulated payment, then the
  purchase in one step. Repeated clicks lead to one sale; a failed payment
  keeps the reservation.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 6
  Commit: 4d3905c fix(sale): prevent timer and inventory state inconsistencies
  What it adds: Fixes 5 real defects found by new full-simulator tests (below).
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 7
  Commit: b741c91 test(sale): add invariant tests and AI failure audit
  What it adds: Randomized operation-sequence tests, the PRD 7 race scenarios,
  and AI_FAILURE_AUDIT.md at the repo root.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: 8
  Commit: 8f3968f docs(sale): finalize mega-sale verification and documentation
  What it adds: An end-to-end test of the whole sale, an architecture table, the

  regression results, and a section in README.md.

  What T-06 fixed. I wrote the integration tests first and ran them against the
  T-05 code; 5 failed:
  - Coming back to the tab: after the lock had run out in the background, the
    panel still showed "Reserved (locked)".
  - Sale end message: "The sale has ended." even though the shopper's
    reservation was still valid and could still be bought.
  - Disabled buttons: none of them said why they were disabled.

  The audit lists 6 failures that the AI (me, in this session) actually produced
  here. Each has the flawed code or draft, the commit or test as evidence, the
  fix and how it was checked:
  - Expiry without a time check: T-03's expire() released stock without checking
    the lock had actually run out.
  - Timer-only expiry: lock expiry relied on timers, with no check when the tab
    came back.
  - Assertions that could never fail: the "nothing on the page changed" checks.
  - Tests that hung instead of failing.
  - Tests that passed for the wrong reason.
  - Misleading UI states: the end-of-sale and disabled-button cases above.

  PRD 7's examples A (a countdown that drifts) and C (checkout without an expiry
  check) never happened in this code. The audit says so plainly instead of
  blaming the AI, and points to the deliberate code breaks that show the tests
  would catch them.

  Checking the tests: after each milestone I broke the code on purpose, about 18
  times in total. Every break made at least one test fail. While doing this I
  also found and fixed two problems in my own new tests: the random test first
  hung, and with instant payments only, it missed a stock leak that happens
  during checkout.

  Decisions to check
  - A lock outlives the sale: a reservation made during the sale can still be
    checked out after the sale ends, until its own lock expires. PRD 6 says the
    sale ending must not erase reserved stock.
  - README: I added a Mega-Sale section to the repo root README.md and left your
    original text above it.
  - Demo additions: two new scenarios ("Live, 20 s lock" and "Starts in 5 s")
    and a "Simulate a failed payment" switch.

  About your two commits. In the same range there are two commits you made whose
  messages don't match what's inside:
  - 02b67d6 reuses the T-01 message but contains the audit files.
  - 0f49cbb has a combined T-02/T-03 message but only deletes LAB2/HW/report.md
    and swaps a PDF.

  I didn't rewrite history; the report notes both. If you want to clean them up,
  they only need their messages changed (for example docs: or chore:), which
  means an interactive rebase that you'd need to run yourself.

